stateDiagram-v2
  state "Legend" as legend {
    lg0: Unmanaged
    lg1: Designated
    lg2: Gateway
    lg3: Breaks NoRefusal or NoSilentLoss
    lg4: Path to the NoRefusal or NoSilentLoss bug
  }
  class lg0 tan
  class lg1 teal
  class lg2 blue
  class lg3 breaks
  class lg4 bugPath
  s0: No owner row, the gateway serves (no node set)
  s1: No owner row, the gateway serves (no node set), an input waits at the gateway
  s2: No owner row, the gateway serves (set to the designated node)
  s3: No owner row, the gateway serves (no node set), turn runs on the gateway
  s4: No owner row, the gateway serves (set to the designated node), an input waits at the gateway
  s5: No owner row, the gateway serves (set to the designated node), turn runs on the gateway
  s6: No owner row, the gateway serves (set to the designated node), an input is kept for the designated node
  s7: No owner row, the gateway serves (set to the designated node), an input waits at the gateway, turn runs on the gateway
  s8: Home is the designated node (set to the designated node), an input is handed to the designated node
  s9: Home is the gateway (set to the designated node), an input is kept for the designated node, turn runs on the gateway (old session)
  s10: Home is the designated node (set to the designated node), turn runs on the designated node
  s11: Home is the gateway (set to the designated node), an input is kept for the designated node, idle session on the gateway [1 input lost]
  s12: Home is the designated node (set to the designated node), an input waits at the gateway, turn runs on the designated node
  s13: Home is the designated node (set to the designated node), an input waits at the gateway, turn runs on the designated node [refusal shown]
  [*] --> s0
  s0 --> s0: an operator edits one node's config file
  s0 --> s1: you send a message
  s0 --> s2: the hub copies its setting to the database
  s1 --> s3: the gateway starts the turn itself
  s2 --> s4: you send a message
  s3 --> s5: the hub copies its setting to the database
  s4 --> s6: the gateway puts the input into shared custody
  s5 --> s7: you send a message
  s6 --> s8: the input is handed to the node that owns the channel
  s7 --> s9: the gateway puts the input into shared custody
  s8 --> s8: a node reads the owner row again
  s9 --> s11: the turn ends and its answer is withheld
  s8 --> s10: the home starts the turn
  s10 --> s12: you send a message
  s12 --> s13: the gateway's writer check refuses before routing
